Orry wrote:
>
> I'm currently on dungeon level 4 and am experience level 5 and have
> passed the branch into the mines.
>
> I'm guessing I should go back to the mines when I am strong enough for
> them?

That depends on your caution and your willingness to retreat up the
stairs to heal.  The mines are crowded and crowds are to be avoided. 
The mines have a lot of monsters for early experience and early
experience is to be pursued.  Quite the condundrum - Do I do the mines
first or Sokoban first?  By the time I've survived both it's the
mid-game and I'm cruising, but there are advantages to doing them in
either order.  I go through phases on which I want to do first.

When I first start the mines I like to cycle up and down the stairs. 
Down, kill one monster, pick up its stuff, up.  Eat the corpse, have the
items checked for danger, maybe use one of the items.  Build up a stash
of items near the stairs.  Heal completely.  Cycle back down.  At some
point the crowd is thinned enough to explore the whole level with only
facing 1-2 monsters at a time.

> And any additional pointers for my race/class?

Eventually the whip becomes worthless because very strong monsters are
immune to it.  Ditch it in favor of a pick axe or mattock (this argues
for doing the mines before Sokoban), then start looking for a silver
saber.

Archeologists can't multi-fire daggers or arrows.  Gather and throw
daggers anyways.  Archeologists can multi-fire rocks from a sling.  That
might not be worth carrying heavy rocks around most of the time but a
pile of rocks prepared at a retreating point in a corridor is not a bad
idea.  Rocks aren't worth carrying around but may be worth placing as a
backup barrage plan.


